          <li><strong>The Core Trade-off:</strong> Medicare Advantage offers <strong>lower monthly premiums ($0 in many counties)</strong> but requires using provider networks and obtaining prior authorizations. Medigap requires a <strong>monthly premium ($130–$250/mo)</strong> but eliminates networks, allows you to see any US doctor who accepts Medicare, and virtually eliminates out-of-pocket copays.</li>
